# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings.
#
# This repo is used on machines with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text
# files to CRLF on checkout. A CRLF shell script has a shebang of
# "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r", and the kernel then looks for an interpreter named
# "bash\r" -- the script fails with "bad interpreter: No such file or
# directory". For .claude/hooks/*.sh that failure would be near-silent: the
# hook simply never runs, which is exactly the invisible-no-fire mode issue
# #354 warns about.
#
# Git hook scripts (.husky/*) hit the same failure mode but have no .sh
# extension by convention, so the rule above misses them entirely -- that
# gap let a CRLF .husky/post-checkout ship in #357/#358 (bash choked on a
# stray \r mid-script instead of a clean interpreter-not-found failure,
# but same root cause).
*.sh text eol=lf
.husky/* text eol=lf
.pnpmfile.cjs text eol=lf
